.TH TILEMAP_AT 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
tilemap_at \- The tile id at tile coordinates tx, ty
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqtilemap.h\(dq
.BI "uint8_t tilemap_at(const Tilemap *m, int tx, int ty);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The tile id at tile coordinates tx, ty. Coordinates outside the map read as 0 (empty), so callers never need bounds checks. Convert a world position first: tilemap_at(m, (int)floorf(wx / m\->tile), (int)floorf(wy / m\->tile)).
.SH RETURN VALUE
the id, 0 outside the map.
.SH MODULE
tilemap (src/engine/tilemap/tilemap.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tilemap_solid_at (3),
.BR Tilemap (3),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge (1)
